I wonder if Prayer could be tweaked to help differentiate classes.
After all, would Loki, the Trickster God, really want to solve
problems in the same way as the warrior gods of the Barbarians, or the
Discworld Gods, or Huan Ti? Shouldn't a warrior god be helpful in
'bringing the pain' by sending forth a minion for the player or
zapping nearby monsters with lightning, but be fairly useless at
curing a stoning attack? Similarly, a follower of Loki could be
assisted by the god's trickery (confusing monsters or causing conflict
if the player is under attack, polymorphing the player into a rock
golem if being stoned) to get out of sticky situations.

Converting to a different God could help bring forward the benefits of
the god's different responses to prayer; Crowning would bring very
different effects for the followers of different gods. The player's
use of gods would then be very different for each character.


